    'egg.stats_hint':   'Click anywhere to close','egg.vendor_comware':'Steady veteran — "show version" takes five seconds to respond','egg.vendor_cisco':'Suited salesman — everything is expensive and needs SMARTnet','egg.vendor_nxos':'Datacenter backbone, high-maintenance, can\'t live without VPC','egg.vendor_aruba':'Campus regular — VSF master, LLDP always on','egg.vendor_procurve':'Retired engineer\'s old pal — stable but EOL','egg.vendor_fortiswitch':'FortiGate\'s obedient child — never disobeys the parent','egg.vendor_juniper':'Academic professor — config looks like a thesis, always says "commit confirmed"','egg.vendor_arista':'Cloud-native pioneer — EOS API more obedient than engineers, Python is mother tongue','egg.vendor_extreme':'STP marathon runner — ExtremeXOS is the secret weapon','egg.vendor_alcatel':'French romance style — OmniSwitch CLI reads like poetry','egg.vendor_brocade':'Classical samurai — FastIron was sharp, now absorbed by Ruckus','egg.vendor_dell-os10':'Dell\'s new generation — OS10 is Linux reincarnated','egg.vendor_routeros':'Flea market Swiss army knife — RouterOS does it all, great value','egg.vendor_ruijie':'Made in China — but why does it look exactly like Cisco?','egg.vendor_netgear':'Known for home routers, but under the hood this line is a proper ICOS switch in disguise','egg.vendor_edgeswitch':'The old guard of the Ubiquiti family — while UniFi went full cloud, this one still holds the line with a serial CLI','egg.vendor_sonic':'Wait, whose kid are YOU, exactly? No single parent — built by a dozen different vendors','egg.vendor_fortigate':'Popular all-in-one firewall — UTM does everything, licensing is a love-hate story','egg.vendor_sophos':'Friendly British gentleman — Synchronized Security lets endpoints chat with the firewall','egg.vendor_checkpoint':'Old-money aristocrat of security — SmartConsole has decades of history, rulebases with thousands of entries','egg.vendor_paloalto':'App-ID pioneer — the class president of NGFW, also the most expensive license','egg.vendor_pfsense':'Honest open-source workhorse — solid FreeBSD roots, free edition rivals commercial products','egg.vendor_opnsense':'pfSense\'s principled fork — community-governed, nothing held back behind a paywall','egg.vendor_sonicwall':'SMB\'s loyal partner — plain UI but surprisingly solid performance','egg.vendor_ciscoasa':'Veteran that transitioned from classic firewall to NGFW — FTD brings a new boss called FMC','egg.vendor_zyxel':'Made in Taiwan — CLI feels like a shrunk enterprise firewall, small but complete','egg.vendor_edgerouter':'Ubiquiti\'s value router — nested-brace syntax traces back to the Vyatta/VyOS bloodline','egg.vendor_openwrt':'King of open-source router firmware — clean stanza format, flashes onto almost anything','egg.vendor_ciscoall':'All-rounder of networking — IOS/NX-OS for switching, ASA/FTD for security, market share unmatched','egg.vendor_arubaall':'HPE\'s dual persona — CX is the cloud-native new generation, ProCurve is the old-school campus favorite','egg.vendor_planet':'Taiwan\'s hidden tech nerd — the CLI apes Cisco convincingly, shows up all over government tenders, yet almost nobody in the industry seems to have heard its name','egg.vendor_watchguard':'A Norse-tier guardian goddess whose necklace Brísingamen is secretly on fire, rides a chariot pulled by cats, and claims first pick of the fallen rules before Valhalla gets the rest',
